class ZimmButton extends HTMLElement {
  static get observedAttributes() {
    return ['variant', 'size', 'label', 'disabled', 'inverse', 'icon', 'type', 'full-width'];
  }

  constructor() {
    super();
    this.attachShadow({ mode: 'open' });
  }

  connectedCallback() { this._render(); }
  attributeChangedCallback(name, oldValue, newValue) { if (oldValue === newValue) return; this._render(); }

  _render() {
    const variant  = this.getAttribute('variant') || 'primary';

    if (variant === 'icon') {
      const icon      = this.getAttribute('icon') || '';
      const type      = this.getAttribute('type') || 'button';
      const label     = this.getAttribute('label') || icon;
      const disabled  = this.hasAttribute('disabled');
      const inv       = this.hasAttribute('inverse');
      const iconBase  = new URL('../icon/assets/', import.meta.url).href;
      const focusColor = inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-white)' : 'var(--zimm-color-border-focus)';

      this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
        <style>
          :host { display: inline-block; }
          button {
            display: inline-flex;
            align-items: center;
            justify-content: center;
            background: none;
            border: none;
            padding: 8px;
            cursor: pointer;
            transition: opacity var(--zimm-motion-duration-fast) var(--zimm-motion-easing-standard);
          }
          button:hover:not(:disabled) { opacity: 0.6; }
          button:disabled { cursor: not-allowed; opacity: 0.4; }
          button:focus-visible {
            outline: 1px solid ${focusColor};
            outline-offset: 2px;
            border-radius: 2px;
          }
          img {
            display: block;
            width: 20px;
            height: 20px;
            ${inv ? 'filter: invert(1);' : ''}
          }
        </style>
        <button type="${type}" ${disabled ? 'disabled' : ''} aria-label="${label}">
          <img src="${iconBase}${icon}.svg" alt="" aria-hidden="true">
        </button>
      `;
      return;
    }


    const size     = this.getAttribute('size') || 'large';
    const label    = this.getAttribute('label') || 'Button';
    const disabled = this.hasAttribute('disabled');
    const inverse  = this.hasAttribute('inverse');

    const p   = variant === 'primary';
    const lg  = size === 'large';
    const inv = inverse;
    const fw  = this.hasAttribute('full-width');

    const bg    = p ? (inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-white)'
                            : 'var(--zimm-color-action-primary-bg-default)')
                    : 'transparent';
    const color = p ? (inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-900)'
                            : 'var(--zimm-color-action-primary-text)')
                    : (inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-white)'
                            : 'var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-text)');
    const border = p ? 'none'
                     : `var(--zimm-border-width-default) solid ${inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-white)' : 'var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-border)'}`;

    const hoverBg          = p ? (inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-ivory-100)' : 'var(--zimm-color-action-primary-bg-hover)')
                               : 'var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-bg-hover)';
    const hoverColor       = p ? (inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-900)' : 'var(--zimm-color-action-primary-text)')
                               : 'var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-text)';
    const hoverBorderColor = !p ? (inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-white)' : 'var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-border)') : '';

    const focusColor  = inv ? 'var(--zimm-color-grey-white)' : 'var(--zimm-color-border-focus)';
    const focusOffset = p ? '2px' : '3px';

    this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
      <style>
        :host { display: inline-block; }
        :host([full-width]) { display: block; width: 100%; }

        button {
          position: relative;
          display: inline-flex;
          ${fw ? 'width: 100%;' : ''}
          align-items: center;
          justify-content: center;
          gap: var(--zimm-size-action-gap);
          min-width: 80px;
          overflow: clip;
          cursor: pointer;
          font-family: var(--zimm-font-family-body);
          font-weight: var(--zimm-font-weight-medium);
          text-transform: uppercase;
          letter-spacing: var(--zimm-font-letterspacing-sm);
          transition: background-color 0.15s ease, color 0.15s ease, border-color 0.15s ease;

          height:      ${lg ? 'var(--zimm-size-action-height-lg)'      : 'var(--zimm-size-action-height-md)'};
          padding:     0 ${lg ? 'var(--zimm-size-action-padding-h-lg)' : 'var(--zimm-size-action-padding-h-md)'};
          font-size:   ${lg ? 'var(--zimm-font-size-2xs)'              : 'var(--zimm-font-size-3xs)'};
          line-height: ${lg ? 'var(--zimm-font-lineheight-3xs)'        : 'var(--zimm-font-lineheight-2xs)'};

          background: ${bg};
          color:      ${color};
          border:     ${border};
        }

        button:hover:not(:disabled) {
          background: ${hoverBg};
          color:      ${hoverColor};
          ${hoverBorderColor ? `border-color: ${hoverBorderColor};` : ''}
        }

        button:active:not(:disabled) {
          background: var(--zimm-color-action-primary-bg-pressed);
          color:      var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-text-inverse);
          ${!p ? 'border-color: var(--zimm-color-action-primary-bg-pressed);' : ''}
        }

        button:focus-visible {
          outline:        var(--zimm-border-width-default) solid ${focusColor};
          outline-offset: ${focusOffset};
        }

        button:disabled {
          cursor:       not-allowed;
          background:   ${p ? 'var(--zimm-color-action-primary-bg-disabled)' : 'transparent'};
          color:        ${p ? 'var(--zimm-color-action-primary-text-disabled)' : 'var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-text-disabled)'};
          border-color: ${p ? 'transparent' : 'var(--zimm-color-action-secondary-text-disabled)'};
        }
      </style>
      <button ${disabled ? 'disabled' : ''}>${label}</button>
    `;
  }
}

customElements.define('zimm-button', ZimmButton);

content.text:
Let me use a real component: `zimm-text-input`, the actual file at `02-design/library/elements/text-input/zimm-text-input.js`. It shows all three day-one blockers at once (format, responsiveness, tokens), plus the form/event problem.

## A. What the workflow produces today (verbatim from the repo)

The relevant parts of the 309-line file:

```js
class ZimmTextInput extends HTMLElement {
  static get observedAttributes() {
    return ['label','placeholder','value','type','name','helper-text','error-text',
            'disabled','inverse','trailing-icon','variant'];   // string attributes only
  }
  connectedCallback() { this._render(); }
  attributeChangedCallback(n,o,v) { if (o===v) return; this._render(); }  // re-renders whole thing

  _render() {
    const value = this.getAttribute('value') || '';
    // ...
    this.shadowRoot.innerHTML = `
      <style>
        .content    { min-height: 36px; }   /* line 126: fixed px */
        .native-input { height: 20px;        /* line 195: fixed px */
                        font-size: var(--zimm-font-size-2xs); }  /* token = fixed 14px */
        .float-label  { line-height: 12px; } /* line 162: fixed px */
        /* ...200+ lines of shadow-DOM CSS... */
      </style>
      <input
        type="${type}"
        value="${value}"                     /* line 277: raw interpolation */
        ${name ? `name="${name}"` : ''}
        ${disabled ? 'disabled' : ''}>
      <label class="float-label">${label}</label>   /* line 272: raw interpolation */
    `;

    // the ONLY listener, and it never leaves the component:
    input.addEventListener('input', (e) => {
      content.classList.toggle('has-value', e.target.value.length > 0);  // line 302-305
    });
  }
}
customElements.define('zimm-text-input', ZimmTextInput);
```

Concretely, what this output cannot do for a React app:

1. **No value out.** The `input` listener (line 302) only toggles a CSS class. Nothing is re-dispatched, and the native event is `composed:false`, so it stays trapped in the shadow root. A React `onChange` on this element **never fires.** There is also no `value` getter on the host, so `ref.current.value` returns nothing useful.
2. **Not a form field.** The host is not form-associated (no `formAssociated`/`attachInternals`), so inside a `<form>` it contributes nothing to submit or `FormData`. For login/address/checkout that means the field does not work.
3. **State gets wiped.** Any attribute change calls `_render()` which resets `shadowRoot.innerHTML` (line 47), destroying the live `<input>`, so the user's typed text, caret, and focus are lost. That is the opposite of how React drives inputs.
4. **Fixed and unsafe.** `36px`/`20px`/`12px` are frozen (lines 126, 195, 162), the type token resolves to a fixed `14px`, and `value="${value}"`/`${label}` are injected raw (XSS). Nothing is fluid, and styling only works if the global `common.css` happens to be loaded on the page.

## B. What we actually need (illustrative target, React)

A controlled React component with a typed API, a real change callback, form participation, safe-by-default rendering, and fluid tokens:

```tsx
// TextInput.tsx  (target output)
import { forwardRef, useId } from 'react';
import styles from './TextInput.module.css';

export interface TextInputProps {
  label: string;
  value: string;
  onChange: (value: string) => void;          // a real callback
  name?: string;
  type?: 'text' | 'email' | 'password' | 'tel';
  helperText?: string;
  error?: string;
  disabled?: boolean;
  variant?: 'flush' | 'outline';
}

export const TextInput = forwardRef<HTMLInputElement, TextInputProps>(
  function TextInput({ label, value, onChange, name, type = 'text', helperText, error, disabled, variant = 'flush' }, ref) {
    const id = useId();
    return (
      <div className={styles.field}>
        <label htmlFor={id} className={styles.label}>{label}</label>
        <input
          ref={ref} id={id} name={name} type={type} value={value} disabled={disabled}
          aria-invalid={!!error}
          className={`${styles.input} ${styles[variant]}`}
          onChange={(e) => onChange(e.target.value)}   // fires; value flows back to React
        />                                              {/* value/label auto-escaped by JSX */}
        {helperText && <p className={styles.help}>{helperText}</p>}
        {error && <p role="alert" className={styles.error}>{error}</p>}
      </div>
    );
  }
);
```

```css
/* TextInput.module.css  (co-located, consumes the shared token layer) */
.input {
  font-size:   var(--zimm-font-size-2xs);          /* token, but now fluid, see below */
  min-height:  clamp(2rem, 1.5rem + 1.5vw, 2.5rem); /* responsive, not 36px */
}
```

And the token layer changes shape so React/TS and the browser both consume it:

```css
/* today  (common.css) */        --zimm-font-size-2xs: 14px;                                  /* fixed */
/* needed (common.css) */        --zimm-font-size-2xs: clamp(0.8125rem, 0.78rem + 0.16vw, 0.875rem); /* fluid */
```
```ts
/* needed additionally: a typed export so the React/TS build can consume tokens */
export const tokens = { fontSize: { '2xs': 'var(--zimm-font-size-2xs)' /* ... */ } } as const;
```

## C. The difference in one place: how a developer consumes it

This is the crux. Same field, both stacks.

```tsx
// TODAY: the web component. Renders, but is inert in React.
<zimm-text-input label="Email" name="email" value={email} />
//  onChange never fires · no value to read back · disabled={false} may not apply
//  in React <=18 · does not submit with the form · value is injected raw
//  -> to get the typed value you hand-wire a listener into el.shadowRoot yourself
```

```tsx
// NEEDED: a real React control that works in a form.
const [email, setEmail] = useState('');
<form onSubmit={handleSubmit}>
  <TextInput label="Email" name="email" type="email"
             value={email} onChange={setEmail} error={errors.email} />
</form>
//  controlled value · onChange fires · submits with the form · TS checks the props
//  · scales with viewport · no injection
```

So the "actual" delta is not cosmetic: today's output is a **self-contained widget that renders a picture of the field**, and what we need is a **React control our app can bind state to and submit.** Multiply this by 27 components. That single transformation (web component to controlled React component), plus the token layer going fluid and gaining a typed export, is the bulk of the hardening work, and precisely the part Han and Ajay already solved on ART Life.

Want me to work this same before/after up for a second component (say `zimm-select`, which adds the JSON-string-props problem, or `zimm-button` for the pure styling/fixed-px angle)?
